  "slug": "current-cosmological-53cb",
  "summary": "Fresh DESI-era analyses test axion and scalar-field dark energy while new BAO and low-z supernova work extends the distance-ladder probes.",
  "synthesis": "Most items test dark energy beyond a fixed positive cosmological constant using current distance and growth data. One analysis constrains axion quintessence with a negative cosmological constant using DES, DESI BAO, CMB and growth data, finding no compelling evidence for a negative value. Another tests a single canonical scalar field with a double-power potential as both early and late dark energy against CMB, DESI BAO and Pantheon+, with the summary noting a raised H0. Complementary probe work reports a BAO measurement in an all-sky cluster catalog and the 2MASS Redshift Survey, consistent with DESI DR2, and proposes a Rubin twilight program for nearby Type Ia supernovae that improves the dark-energy figure of merit in simulations. The decihertz eccentric IMRI paper is a gravitational-wave template-bias study and is not part of this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
